      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE ART OF SUCCESS (9) has been powering through her grades and stretched her winning run to eight when beating the boys by 3.4m at Melton last start. Freshened since but is well placed against her own sex and while drawn on the back row she has won from there before. Unbeaten mare HOUSE PARTY (10) is the big query. Hasn't raced for 11 months but was impressive in winning her only two starts by big margins. Tricky draw but she hails from a premier yard. WICKED CONFESSION (8) is two from this time in and showed her talent when placed in the Queen Elizabeth II Mile at Menangle last campaign. Strikes at 50 per cent at this distance and draws for a trail. PEACE OUT (11) cops a second row draw but but she is capable and should be ready to go off a couple of trials. LUV THE NITELIFE (7) draws wide but her best form would measure up here.",
